data bare_variant_elected_by_spelling_not_by_expected_coproduct: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "bare_variant_elected_by_spelling_not_by_expected_coproduct" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a bare variant spelling in VALUE position is elected to a coproduct by its spelling alone, ignoring the expected type -- `Absent` passed to a ConvergeVerdict parameter (gunbc.host_converge) in a module that sees ConvergeVerdict and ObservationVerdict (std.upsert_decision), both declaring Absent, without importing either. The closure-wide unique-spelling tier dropped the ambiguous spelling and the kernel tier filled it with the kernel Optional's Absent, so the reference was typed as an Optional at a Required position. A second shape of the same state: a coproduct arm reached only through the generic global binding lookup typed as a plain variable, with no VariantValueBinding, which the interpreter answers NoSuchVariable at run time.",
    "HARM: the wrong owner was elected silently. gunbc#12791's optional-at-required wall then REFUSED those correct programs, a fabricated refusal (16 sites in gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_cli and gunbc.file_access, 6 in test.claim.fleet.fleet_converge_cli_witness_test), and #12791 shipped a predicate exclusion for them. No WRONG VALUE is observed shipped: the interpreter matches arms by spelling, so the kernel-elected Absent compared equal to the declared one at run time -- correct by coincidence, which is why the election error was invisible to every by-execution claim (test.claim.variant_election_by_expected_coproduct_witness_test row 4 is green on the unrepaired seed too; row 1, which asserts the emitted constructor, is the discriminator).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent wrongness masked by a predicate exclusion. RUNG NOW (gunbc#12902): structurally guaranteed on the v1 value route where an expected type exists -- v1.compiler.infer expected_deciding_variant_owner elects the expected coproduct's arm first (an Optional-cardinality expected decides Optional's own arms); a spelling the closure tier finds ambiguous never falls through to the kernel (merge_kernel_variant_locals_low_priority) and refuses AmbiguousReference where no expected type decides; kernel ties bind neither; and a coproduct arm reached only by the global binding lookup refuses at typecheck (variant_outside_declared_scope_refusal). Pattern position was never affected: lookup_variant_in_type elects by the scrutinee's type.",
    "CEILING AND NEXT TRIGGER: the closure-unique tier remains as the STAND-IN for the module's declared scope (own module plus explicit imports), so an unimported arm still binds by closure-unique spelling. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: quiet-hawk-702's Node.declaration cut installs the declared scope as v1.compiler.infer build_ancestry_precedence and DELETES the closure-wide variant tier and its threading, so election reads only own declarations, explicit imports, the expected coproduct and the kernel.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
